|> Exercise
    work=ing
    handle=_ab_inequality_
    
    Prove that

    |> Boxed
        $$
        \huge a^2 + b^2 \geq 2ab
        $$

    for all $a, b \in \rr$.

    |> Solution

        !! This is a one-line proof (oops 
        !! |> del
        !!     two
        !! three lines):
        We have

        $$
        \begin{aligned}
        & a^2 + b^2 \geq 2ab \\
        \iff & \up{1.5} a^2 - 2ab + b^2 \geq 0 \\
        \iff & \up{1.5} (a - b)^2 \geq 0
        \end{aligned}
        $$

        where the last inequality is true because the
        square of any real number is nonnegative, and,
        therefore, the first inequality is true. (Recall
        that 
        $$
        \te{“}\!\!\iff\!\!\te{”}
        $$
        means “if and only if”.)

        !! Where we recall that
        !! $$
        !! \te{“}\!\iff\!\te{”}
        !! $$
        !! means “if and only if”, and where the last
        !! inequality is true because the square of anything
        !! (certainly of any real number) is nonnegative.

        !! |> SolutionNote

        !!     This inequality has a kind of geometric
        !!     proof:

        |> SolutionNote

            One can also note that

            !! $$
            !! \begin{aligned}
            !! & a^2 + b^2 = 2ab \\
            !! \iff & \up{1.5} a^2 - 2ab + b^2 = 0 \\
            !! \iff & \up{1.5} (a - b)^2 = 0 \\
            !! \iff & \up{1.5} a = b
            !! \end{aligned}
            !! $$
            $$
            \begin{aligned}
            & a^2 + b^2 > 2ab \\
            \iff & \up{1.5} a^2 - 2ab + b^2 > 0 \\
            \iff & \up{1.5} (a - b)^2 > 0 \\
            \iff & \up{1.5} a \ne b
            \end{aligned}
            $$

            which means that $a^2 + b^2$ is 

            !! $$
            !! a^2 + b^2
            !! $$

            __strictly greater__

            than $2ab$ except in one case and in one case only:
            the case that $a$ equals $b$.
            (In which case, indeed, $a^2 + b^2 = 2a^2 = 2ab$.)
            !! Note that

            !! $$
            !! a^2 + b^2 > 2ab
            !! $$

            !! if and only if

            !! $$
            !! (a - b)^2 > 0
            !! $$

            !! because we can replay the above derivation
            !! with “$>$” instead of “$\geq$”. But